:synohw_hw_plug:
> **What this is.** Everything this DS2415+ (and a DX1215 behind it) tells Linux about itself, read-only: `/sys` and `/proc` files, plus a small cache in `/var/run/synology-hardware/inventory` that the daemon refreshes every `INVENTORY_PERIOD` seconds (600 by default; `rc.synology-hardware inventory` refreshes it at once). The cache holds what needs a command: `smartctl -n standby -i -H -A -l error -l sataphy` for the disks Unraid reports awake, and `ethtool <port>` for Wake-on-LAN. A disk in standby is never queried, and `-n standby` makes smartctl skip one that fell asleep in the meantime, so this section can never wake a disk. The page itself runs no command.
>
> **Sources.** The choice of items, how each was measured on this unit and why the rest is left out: `research/2026-10-25-hw-info-inventory.md` (the "#n" numbers in the notes refer to its table), raw outputs in `experiments/2026-10-25-hw-inventory/`. The "Not available" table is checked live where a file can tell (e.g. `/sys/devices/system/edac` absent) and says so if that ever changes.
>
> **Refresh.** Page load, then every 60 s; the 5 s live poll does not touch this section.
:end
